! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F211 "STORE LOW ORDER
! TEST ROUTINE", "ARITHMETIC CHECKS F211A", sub-tests A1-A2
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.113, octal 016144.40-016163.00,
! where F211A3 begins).
!
! The diagnostic that drives SLO (STORE LOW ORDER, opcode 1001110),
! which decodes but has no execute arm -- exactly the position SRD was
! in before F210.
!
! What the manual says (Ref. Manual p.97). "The low-order part of a
! double-length accumulator fraction with appropriate exponent is
! placed in the location specified by the effective address." The
! fraction is accumulator bits 60-107 -- the LOW half -- and "the
! exponent is obtained by SUBTRACTING 48 from the exponent in bits
! 0-11 of the accumulator". Normalized, the low-order fraction is
! shifted left until a one is leftmost, and "if noisy mode is also
! specified, ONES are entered from the right during the normalization
! shifting; otherwise zeros" -- unlike SRD, where noisy mode does not
! affect the operation at all. The accumulator sign as modified, and
! the accumulator flag bits (sign byte 4-7), go to storage bits 60-63.
! The accumulator and sign byte remain unchanged.
!
! Two special cases. When the ACCUMULATOR exponent is flagged, "the
! same exponent is set with the low-order fraction when stored", the
! indicators are for propagated flags, and normalization is
! suppressed. When the exponent WITH THE LOW ORDER FRACTION has EF of
! 1 as a result of the operation -- that is, when subtracting 48
! underflows -- the indicators are for generated flags and
! "normalization, if specified, in this case DOES occur".
!
! A1 and A2 are both the flagged case, so neither exercises the -48 --
! the same shape F210A1-A2 had for SRD, and for the same reason: they
! are the clean first test.
!
!   A1  DL(U) FK40 (XFP +1023, sign 1) with C0011 dropping FK23's
!       fraction aaaaaaaaaaaa into the low half. SLO(U) stores that
!       low half with the accumulator's own exponent, which is exactly
!       FK23's exponent and fraction. BB then checks the stored sign
!       bit is 1, FK40's sign.
!   A2  the same in XFN with FK25 and FK30, expecting FK30, and BZB
!       checking the stored sign is 0.
!
! Transcribed as printed: A2's comment reads "ACC EXP IN XFP RNG"
! where FK25 decodes to XFN -767. A1's says the same and FK40 really
! is XFP. The listing repeated the comment; the constants are what
! they are.
!
! A1 opens with Z,$IND, clearing the indicator register before the
! operation -- the first block in this series to do so.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant.
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.178. PASS sits at 016163.00, where F211A3 begins.
!
! Instructions: DL(U), Z, C0011, SLO(U), L, CT0110, SIC, BB, BZB,
! BRGZ, B.
! verify_fp_arith_f211a1_2_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.178) --
        SLC, (8)022171.0
FK23    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777525252525252525240
        SLC, (8)022173.0
FK25    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577777777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022200.0
FK30    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577617777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022212.0
FK40    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777577777777777777770

! The listing labels 016144.40 SAP12, an SSIP prologue target rather
! than this block's own name; ENTRY is ours, needed only as the END
! operand.
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)16144.40
ENTRY   DL(U), FK40                            ! F211A1: acc exp in XFP rng
        Z, $IND
        C0011(BU,48), FK23+.12, 20
        SLO(U), ROS
        L(BU), FK23
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                  ! was fract stored with mem,exp+acc.exp
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BB, ROS+.60, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        DL(U), FK25                            ! F211A2: acc exp in XFN rng (printed XFP)
        C0011(BU,48), FK30+.12, 20
        SLO(U), ROS
        L(BU), FK30
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, ROS+.60, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                                 ! 016163.00: where F211A3 begins
        END, ENTRY
